# =====================================================================
# Direct dependencies for <YOUR MODEL NAME> evaluation wrapper
#
# WHEN TO UPDATE:
#   - When you add a new import in dataloader.py, inference.py, or
#     postprocess.py that isn't already covered below.
#   - When a dependency version causes a conflict inside the container.
#
# HOW TO UPDATE:
#   1. Add or change the package spec here (e.g. my-pkg>=1.2.0).
#   2. Re-compile the pinned lockfile:
#        pip install pip-tools
#        pip-compile requirements.in -o requirements.txt --no-header
#      Or if using uv (recommended):
#        uv pip compile requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#   3. Rebuild the Docker image so the new requirements.txt is picked up.
#
# NOTE: If your model ships its own pyproject.toml / setup.py (e.g. a
#   cloned repo managed by uv), its dependencies are handled separately
#   by `uv sync` inside the Dockerfile. Only list packages here that are
#   needed by the evaluation wrapper scripts (dataloader/inference/
#   postprocess) and are NOT already pulled in by the model's own deps.
# =====================================================================

